# Ownership for the paths where a mistake reboots a node or disarms the check
# that would have caught it.
#
# @fam-melcher is an organisation, and an organisation cannot own code — GitHub
# requires a user or a team — so the owner is spelled as the user.
#
# One maintainer means "require review from Code Owners" cannot be satisfied on
# main: GitHub does not accept a pull request's author as its approver. Until a
# second maintainer exists this file is documentation and notification, and the
# branch protection that actually enforces is the required status checks
# (ADR 0013).

*                           @Vonor

# The guards, their self-tests, and the workflows that run them. A pull request
# can edit these and the job still reports success — see the merge-base note in
# .github/workflows/nodeop-guard.yml.
/.github/                   @Vonor

# Privileged node operations. A merged manifest here has ArgoCD create a
# NodeOpUpgrade, which runs a privileged, HostPID container with the host
# filesystem mounted on the targeted node, and reboots it.
/clusters/*/upgrades/       @Vonor
/base/kairos-operator/      @Vonor
